# Git: track only Python and Markdown (plus essential root metadata); exclude temp/outputs and large binaries
# 1) Ignore everything
*

# 2) Allow directory traversal (so we can whitelist files inside)
!*/

# 3) Allow code and docs everywhere
!**/*.py
!**/*.md

# 4) Allow essential root files
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!pyproject.toml
!requirements*.txt
!.cursorignore
!.cursorindexingignore
!README.md
!CLAUDE.md
!LICENSE
!pyrightconfig.json
!.specify
!RL-refactoring-plan
!RL-refactoring-plan/**


# 5) Exclude temporary/experimental and large output directories (even if they contain .py/.md)
temporal/**
outputs/**
output-*/**
output-post/**
model_cache/**
data/**
ds_*/**
infer_results/**
tb/**
logs/**
tmp/**
temp/**
.venv/**
.env/**
__pycache__/**
.cache/**
.ipynb_checkpoints/**
tests_back/**
src_new_bak/**
patents/**
mcp/**
legacy/**
logs/**
.claude/**
test_back/**
AI研发工作汇报.md

# 6) Re-ignore large/binary artifacts
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.safetensors
**/*.ckpt
**/*.bin
**/*.h5
**/*.onnx
**/*.tar
**/*.zip
**/*.7z
**/*.gz
**/*.bz2
**/*.xz
**/*.jpeg
**/*.jpg
**/*.png
**/*.webp
**/*.gif
